%% Line tool lifecycle state diagram: first-drag and two-tap paths
stateDiagram-v2
  [*] --> Idle

  state "Idle / no pending line" as Idle
  note right of Idle
    No pending start, line preview, line commit intent,
    or pointer-owned line overlay exists.
  end note

  Idle --> FirstTapGate: finite first tap in line tool
  Idle --> Idle: non-line tool, invalid tap, or stale sample / ignore
  Idle --> Disposed: runtime.dispose()

  state "First tap admission" as FirstTapGate
  note right of FirstTapGate
    The first pointer down stores finite start facts, current
    tool, and current document/controller epoch. A terminal up
    within tap slop stores pending start for the two-tap path;
    a move outside tap slop becomes the first-drag path. Neither
    path creates a line element, commit intent, action, or document
    signal before a terminal endpoint decision.
  end note

  FirstTapGate --> PendingStart: start finite and tool style drawable / store pending start, publish overlay pending marker
  FirstTapGate --> LinePreview: finite move beyond tap slop / convert active first-tap session to endpoint preview
  FirstTapGate --> Idle: non-finite start, non-drawable style, or inactive surface / no commit
  FirstTapGate --> Disposed: disposed runtime / StateError

  state "Pending start / epoch-bound" as PendingStart
  note right of PendingStart
    Pending line state outlives unrelated pointer-session
    terminal cleanup and interactive=false when no active
    routed pointer owns it. Only line-owned cleanup,
    mode/tool change, prepared load cleanup, cancel, dispose,
    or terminal line decision may clear it.
  end note

  PendingStart --> LinePreview: finite pointer move with same tool and controllerEpoch / overlay line preview only
  PendingStart --> SecondTapGate: finite second tap
  PendingStart --> CleanupOnly: cancel, mode/tool change, or loadDocument prepared cleanup before install
  PendingStart --> PendingStart: loadDocumentFromJson failure / preserve pending start and preview
  PendingStart --> PendingStart: interactive=false with no active routed pointer / disable future routing only; preserve pending start
  PendingStart --> PendingStart: unrelated pointer cleanup or stale non-terminal sample / preserve pending start
  PendingStart --> DisposeCleanup: runtime.dispose()

  state "Line preview / overlay only" as LinePreview
  note right of LinePreview
    Preview facts are immutable overlay state. No selected-move
    main-scene preview, resolver call, Store mutation, spatial
    update, projection eviction, action, or document effect is
    allowed while previewing. Preview changes publish
    CanvasRuntimeState through state.revisions.preview.
  end note

  LinePreview --> LinePreview: finite move with same tool and controllerEpoch / replace overlay preview end
  LinePreview --> SecondTapGate: finite second tap or active-drag terminal up
  LinePreview --> CleanupOnly: cancel, mode/tool change, or loadDocument prepared cleanup before install
  LinePreview --> LinePreview: loadDocumentFromJson failure / preserve pending line
  LinePreview --> LinePreview: interactive=false with no active routed pointer / disable future routing only; preserve line preview
  LinePreview --> LinePreview: unrelated pointer cleanup or stale non-terminal sample / preserve preview
  LinePreview --> DisposeCleanup: runtime.dispose()

  state "Endpoint terminal gate" as SecondTapGate
  note right of SecondTapGate
    A terminal endpoint may create a commit intent only when the
    pending start or active drag endpoint still exists, tool and
    controllerEpoch match, start/end are finite, and style facts
    remain valid.
  end note

  SecondTapGate --> CleanupOnly: no pending start, controllerEpoch mismatch, tool mismatch, invalid terminal, or non-finite facts
  SecondTapGate --> CommitIntent: same tool and controllerEpoch with finite start/end and valid style facts

  state "Line commit intent" as CommitIntent
  note right of CommitIntent
    InteractionEngine returns a line commit intent to
    RuntimeRoot. RuntimeRoot reads the current non-mutating
    Store candidate immediately before it constructs the
    CanvasLineElement and prepares the synchronous EditKernel
    request. Accepted Store-ledger admission reserves the ID;
    failure/no-op leaves it next. InteractionEngine does
    not mutate DocumentStoreKernel directly and does not
    publish drawLine before commit success.
  end note

  CommitIntent --> EditKernelOutcome: RuntimeRoot opens interaction edit and stages drawLine action descriptor

  state "EditKernel outcome" as EditKernelOutcome
  note right of EditKernelOutcome
    Atomic install is the only commit boundary. Rollback,
    rejected Future, stale handle, preflight failure, or exception
    leaves committed document revisions, spatial index,
    projection cache, main repaint, and drawLine action unchanged.
  end note

  EditKernelOutcome --> SuccessfulCommit: atomic install accepted
  EditKernelOutcome --> CleanupOnly: rollback, rejection, preflight failure, or exception

  state "Successful commit installed" as SuccessfulCommit
  SuccessfulCommit --> CleanupAfterCommit: close edit session and mark pending line cleared

  state "Cleanup after successful commit" as CleanupAfterCommit
  note right of CleanupAfterCommit
    Pending start and overlay preview are cleared through the
    PointerToolCleanupCoordinator before public CanvasRuntimeState,
    action, and repaint effects are observed.
  end note

  CleanupAfterCommit --> CleanupCoordinator: typed cleanup request after successful commit

    state "Publish successful commit signals" as PublishCommitSignals
    note right of PublishCommitSignals
    RuntimeRoot enters one guard after cleanup and delivers spatial,
    resource/session release, root/bridged frame, one
    CanvasRuntimeState with document and preview revisions,
    drawLine, then a non-empty observer.
  end note
  PublishCommitSignals --> Idle: signals published

  state "Cleanup only / no committed effects" as CleanupOnly
  note left of CleanupOnly
    Creates a typed cleanup request for pending start, active
    first-tap, and line overlay preview only. No line
    element, document effect, drawLine action, spatial delta,
    projection eviction, or main-scene preview is produced.
    previewRevision advances and publishes CanvasRuntimeState only
    when pending preview was visible.
  end note
  CleanupOnly --> CleanupCoordinator: line-owned cleanup request

  state "PointerToolCleanupCoordinator" as CleanupCoordinator
  note left of CleanupCoordinator
    Coordinator-owned line cleanup uses request ownership context
    to clear line-owned pending state and preserve non-owned
    pending line state on interactive=false. It returns an
    effect-only PointerCleanupOutcome and emits no drawLine action.
  end note
  CleanupCoordinator --> OverlayCleanup: outcome says pending overlay was visible
  CleanupCoordinator --> Idle: outcome says no visible overlay
  CleanupCoordinator --> PublishCommitSignals: post-success cleanup outcome

  state "Overlay cleanup repaint" as OverlayCleanup
  OverlayCleanup --> Idle: overlay cleanup published
  OverlayCleanup --> Disposed: dispose cleanup published before stream close

  state "Dispose cleanup" as DisposeCleanup
  note left of DisposeCleanup
    Runtime disposal clears pending line and preview,
    queues overlay cleanup, then closes streams.
    Later samples cannot revive or commit it.
  end note
  DisposeCleanup --> CleanupCoordinator: typed cleanup request before stream close

  state "Disposed runtime" as Disposed
  Disposed --> Disposed: later pointer/edit operation / StateError
  Disposed --> Disposed: dispose() again / no side effects

  note left of CommitIntent
    Negative invariants:
    no selected-move resolver;
    no selected-move main-scene preview;
    no direct Store mutation;
  end note
